In the diagram $BD \parallel AE$. Which test proves that $\Delta CBD \sim \Delta CAE$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.85]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.8,0);
\coordinate (E) at (0.3,2.6);
\coordinate (D) at (2.175,1.516);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (A) -- (E);
\draw (E) -- (C);
\draw (B) -- (D);
\draw[->] ($(A)!0.45!(E)$) -- ($(A)!0.6!(E)$);
\draw[->] ($(B)!0.45!(D)$) -- ($(B)!0.6!(D)$);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above right] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above left] at (E) {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

