The two triangles are equiangular, with the equal angles marked. Which similarity statement writes the vertices in matching order?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.8,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0.75,1.9);
\draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.45cm] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.38cm] {angle=A--B--C};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.5cm] {angle=A--B--C};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\coordinate (E) at (4.2,0);
\coordinate (D) at (8.0,0);
\coordinate (F) at (5.019,2.581);
\draw (E) -- (D) -- (F) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.45cm] {angle=D--E--F};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.38cm] {angle=F--D--E};
\pic[draw,angle radius=0.5cm] {angle=F--D--E};
\node[below left] at (E) {$E$};
\node[below right] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above] at (F) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the diagram $DE \parallel BC$, with $AD = 3$, $DB = 6$ and $DE = 4$. Find $BC$.
